This licence covers the CODE in this repository only.

It does NOT cover the CSV the code produces. That file is a derivative of
whichever sources you chose to fetch, and it inherits their terms. Two of the
optional archives make the result undistributable: hwaitt is CC BY-NC 4.0, so a
build including it cannot be used commercially, and the ayuser Japanese archive
states no licence at all, so there is no grant to redistribute a derivative of
it. Delete those two zips from raw/ before building if you intend to publish or
sell what comes out.

Even a build without them mixes CC BY-SA (Wikipedia) with CDLA-Sharing-1.0
(the deltaromeo archive). Both are share-alike, so a published build carries
share-alike terms and attribution obligations. One further caveat on that
archive: it is uploaded as CDLA-Sharing-1.0, but its schema is Racing Post
shaped, so the uploader may not have held the rights they granted.

Work out what applies to your build before you republish it. See the Sources
table in README.md for the licence on every input.
